1
00:00:38,730 --> 00:00:41,030
Star...

2
00:00:52,770 --> 00:00:55,070
"You told me to trust what you were doing."

3
00:00:58,130 --> 00:01:00,430
This is my whole life we're talking about!

4
00:01:01,730 --> 00:01:04,200
It's okay, Mii. I'll be right here with you.

5
00:01:05,670 --> 00:01:07,700
Then tell me what you want me to do.

6
00:01:07,700 --> 00:01:09,630
You want an answer that badly?

7
00:01:10,230 --> 00:01:11,670
Right now, I don't even want to see your face.

8
00:01:13,100 --> 00:01:13,900
Just go. Wherever.

9
00:01:14,730 --> 00:01:16,470
You're so fucking selfish.

10
00:04:01,970 --> 00:04:04,070
Oh, shit. It's 7:30.

11
00:04:06,670 --> 00:04:08,100
Physics! Physics!

12
00:04:14,000 --> 00:04:16,170
Ow! What'd you kick me for, Fuen?!

13
00:04:16,170 --> 00:04:18,170
It's 7:30! First day of school!

14
00:04:18,970 --> 00:04:21,200
You said if you slept over, we wouldn't be late!

15
00:04:21,200 --> 00:04:22,000
Ugh.

16
00:04:25,100 --> 00:04:26,100
Oh, shit.

17
00:04:27,800 --> 00:04:29,400
We're fucked. It's 7:30.

18
00:04:32,270 --> 00:04:33,270
Shower!

19
00:04:36,630 --> 00:04:37,870
I'm showering first!

20
00:04:37,870 --> 00:04:40,000
Hey, wait for me!

21
00:06:22,100 --> 00:06:23,100
Oh, you two.

22
00:06:23,100 --> 00:06:24,570
Heading out already?

23
00:06:24,570 --> 00:06:25,830
Morning, Mom.

24
00:06:25,830 --> 00:06:26,700
Morning, dear.

25
00:06:27,870 --> 00:06:28,800
Move, move.

26
00:06:36,500 --> 00:06:37,430
Hold this.

27
00:06:39,870 --> 00:06:40,770
Here.

28
00:06:50,900 --> 00:06:51,800
Hey!

29
00:06:51,800 --> 00:06:53,270
Stop hogging my bike!

30
00:06:53,870 --> 00:06:57,270
Quit whining. Get on and hold tight. Hurry.

31
00:07:02,430 --> 00:07:05,130
Drive safe, boys. And study hard, okay?

32
00:07:05,130 --> 00:07:06,170
Yes, ma'am!

33
00:07:06,170 --> 00:07:07,870
Tuition's not cheap!

34
00:07:07,870 --> 00:07:09,270
We know!

35
00:07:45,230 --> 00:07:46,230
Whoa.

36
00:07:46,230 --> 00:07:47,470
He's so cool.

37
00:07:53,200 --> 00:07:55,030
Stop! Stop right there!

38
00:07:55,030 --> 00:07:56,300
Get in line!

39
00:07:57,000 --> 00:07:59,230
Wow, late on the very first day, huh?

40
00:08:00,570 --> 00:08:02,300
Physics—it's Jamesphorn!

41
00:08:02,300 --> 00:08:03,430
Get to the back.

42
00:08:06,300 --> 00:08:08,200
These kids, honestly.

43
00:08:08,200 --> 00:08:10,070
I really hate having to be the strict one.

44
00:08:34,000 --> 00:08:36,299
Come on up. Careful climbing.

45
00:08:38,400 --> 00:08:41,100
Yeah, I never learn—do the same thing every time.

46
00:08:44,330 --> 00:08:45,570
Careful! That's dangerous!

47
00:08:49,730 --> 00:08:51,830
Oh—Din!

48
00:08:54,670 --> 00:08:56,770
Hey, Din!

49
00:09:03,530 --> 00:09:05,070
Fuen, are you okay?

50
00:09:05,430 --> 00:09:06,330
Are you hurt anywhere?

51
00:09:06,330 --> 00:09:08,870
Stop spinning me, I'm dizzy. I'm fine.

52
00:09:11,330 --> 00:09:12,130
Okay.

53
00:09:12,430 --> 00:09:13,430
Oh—

54
00:09:13,730 --> 00:09:15,230
Mr. Student Council President.

55
00:09:16,600 --> 00:09:19,100
Sorry, forgot to say hi. Didn't see you.

56
00:09:19,100 --> 00:09:21,930
You and Fuen better hurry to the hall.

57
00:09:22,200 --> 00:09:23,400
The principal's still stuck in a meeting.

58
00:09:23,400 --> 00:09:25,200
You might make it before they close the doors.

59
00:09:25,200 --> 00:09:26,900
Jamesphorn's in charge right now, too.

60
00:09:26,900 --> 00:09:28,230
I won't be able to help much.

61
00:09:28,530 --> 00:09:29,900
Okay. Thanks a lot, man.

62
00:09:30,430 --> 00:09:31,370
See you.

63
00:09:42,000 --> 00:09:43,530
Hey, Fuen! Physics!

64
00:09:43,530 --> 00:09:46,000
Late again? You guys are so damn cool!

65
00:09:46,000 --> 00:09:48,970
Thanks, kid! Now get to class, don't dawdle.

66
00:10:41,330 --> 00:10:42,200
Hey!

67
00:10:42,900 --> 00:10:43,770
Whoa!

68
00:10:47,370 --> 00:10:48,630
That's a lot.

69
00:10:49,470 --> 00:10:50,330
Hello? Bro?

70
00:10:51,200 --> 00:10:52,000
What's up?

71
00:10:52,200 --> 00:10:53,630
Don't "what's up" me!

72
00:10:53,630 --> 00:10:55,000
The doors are about to close!

73
00:10:55,000 --> 00:10:56,970
Yeah, yeah, I'm hurrying!

74
00:11:03,570 --> 00:11:05,870
What's all this noise, students?

75
00:11:06,500 --> 00:11:08,230
Get ready to head into the hall.

76
00:11:08,630 --> 00:11:10,570
Keep it up and you'll all be on probation.

77
00:11:12,430 --> 00:11:14,500
And fix your uniforms.

78
00:11:17,470 --> 00:11:20,630
You tell me not to be late—look at you, bro.

79
00:11:21,000 --> 00:11:24,900
If Mom finds out you made Fuen late again, she'll nag your ears off.

80
00:11:24,900 --> 00:11:26,130
Hey—don't tell Mom, then.

81
00:11:26,130 --> 00:11:29,000
Talking while running is exhausting, okay? Gotta go.

82
00:11:29,000 --> 00:11:30,100
Gotta go.

83
00:11:34,070 --> 00:11:35,500
Oh—Physics.

84
00:12:13,800 --> 00:12:14,900
What are you all looking for?

85
00:12:14,900 --> 00:12:17,970
Hold on, I still can't find my idol.

86
00:12:17,970 --> 00:12:19,070
Help me look.

87
00:12:19,070 --> 00:12:19,670
Your idol?

88
00:12:19,670 --> 00:12:20,270
Yeah.

89
00:12:20,500 --> 00:12:22,300
You take the front, I'll take the back.

90
00:12:22,300 --> 00:12:23,100
Okay.

91
00:12:23,930 --> 00:12:24,930
I've got the right side.

92
00:12:24,930 --> 00:12:27,130
He's still not here—he's definitely late.

93
00:12:27,130 --> 00:12:28,070
Oh, please.

94
00:12:28,600 --> 00:12:30,070
Don't badmouth my idol.

95
00:12:30,070 --> 00:12:32,270
A guy like Aof is never late.

96
00:12:33,670 --> 00:12:35,170
He's still not here, though.

97
00:12:54,830 --> 00:12:56,970
I don't think we should go in yet.

98
00:12:58,100 --> 00:13:00,770
I don't want toilet duty on day one.

99
00:13:04,930 --> 00:13:08,030
Yeah, agreed.

100
00:13:08,030 --> 00:13:11,170
Let's just get out of here, then.

101
00:13:21,930 --> 00:13:24,430
Hey, hey—

102
00:13:28,030 --> 00:13:29,930
Aof—Aof—damn it, Aof!

103
00:13:41,630 --> 00:13:43,730
Is this my jinx year or what?

104
00:13:44,300 --> 00:13:46,000
Jinx year? I don't know about that.

105
00:13:46,000 --> 00:13:47,770
But I'm definitely done being friends with you.

106
00:13:47,770 --> 00:13:48,830
Same here. / Oh, boy.

107
00:13:48,830 --> 00:13:49,670
Here she comes.

108
00:13:50,570 --> 00:13:51,570
Akkharawit! / Yes, ma'am.

109
00:13:51,570 --> 00:13:52,470
Tinnaphat! / Yes, ma'am.

110
00:13:52,470 --> 00:13:53,200
Physics!

111
00:13:53,200 --> 00:13:54,700
Why are you all this late?

112
00:13:54,700 --> 00:13:55,800
Go sit down.

113
00:13:55,800 --> 00:13:56,900
Yes, ma'am.

114
00:14:00,330 --> 00:14:01,670
Why so late?

115
00:14:03,530 --> 00:14:04,400
Point at who?

116
00:14:05,230 --> 00:14:06,100
Physics.

117
00:14:22,130 --> 00:14:25,230
Hello, students. Everyone's all smiles today.

118
00:14:25,230 --> 00:14:27,930
For the start of this new school term—

119
00:14:27,930 --> 00:14:32,130
our M.4 students may be thrilled about their new uniforms,

120
00:14:32,830 --> 00:14:35,600
and the freedom of a new hairstyle.

121
00:14:35,600 --> 00:14:38,470
You're all about to learn and experience

122
00:14:38,470 --> 00:14:40,500
so many more fun activities.

123
00:14:41,500 --> 00:14:46,470
I hope every one of you lives life to the fullest

124
00:14:46,470 --> 00:14:48,330
and truly enjoys every moment.

125
00:14:49,200 --> 00:14:52,730
As for our M.5 students, you may feel that this year

126
00:14:52,730 --> 00:14:55,700
isn't a year of big changes.

127
00:14:55,700 --> 00:14:57,030
But trust me—

128
00:14:57,030 --> 00:15:01,230
being the middle year, you'll carry more responsibility.

129
00:15:01,230 --> 00:15:04,370
It may be the year you find a new path,

130
00:15:04,370 --> 00:15:08,900
and a clearer goal for your own future.

131
00:15:09,870 --> 00:15:12,700
I hope you'll use this precious time

132
00:15:12,700 --> 00:15:15,730
as wisely as you possibly can.

133
00:15:15,730 --> 00:15:19,300
And thank you for always bringing the school honor.

134
00:15:20,230 --> 00:15:23,700
And our M.6 seniors, the eldest of this house—

135
00:15:23,700 --> 00:15:28,930
who'll soon head off to places far bigger than here—

136
00:15:28,930 --> 00:15:34,000
I want to see you all chase your dreams and do what you set your hearts on.

137
00:15:34,000 --> 00:15:37,530
Even if you stumble, or get so tired you want to quit,

138
00:15:37,530 --> 00:15:41,230
I hope you still find joy in what you do.

139
00:15:41,230 --> 00:15:46,530
Even facing setbacks, keep smiling and be proud of yourselves—

140
00:15:46,530 --> 00:15:50,000
for being strong enough to make it this far.

141
00:15:50,500 --> 00:15:54,400
I believe the life and the path you choose

142
00:15:54,400 --> 00:15:56,600
will never be the wrong one.

143
00:15:56,600 --> 00:16:00,870
Because it's the path you chose for yourselves.

144
00:16:00,870 --> 00:16:06,070
So be proud, and make the most of your final year in this house.

145
00:16:06,070 --> 00:16:08,230
All you sons of this house.

146
00:16:08,600 --> 00:16:09,770
And finally—

147
00:16:09,770 --> 00:16:14,130
A Thapfah boy never makes someone love him then walks away.

148
00:16:14,130 --> 00:16:18,430
A Thapfah boy takes your hand and your heart, and walks on with you.

149
00:16:53,070 --> 00:16:54,830
Hey, hey—

150
00:16:57,170 --> 00:17:00,700
This term, you three are gonna see a lot of me.

151
00:17:00,700 --> 00:17:04,730
Hey, hey—look happy about it.

152
00:17:04,730 --> 00:17:05,869
Yay...

153
00:17:06,500 --> 00:17:07,970
You're teaching us, ma'am?

154
00:17:20,430 --> 00:17:21,630
Whoa.

155
00:17:27,630 --> 00:17:28,830
Whoa.

156
00:17:28,830 --> 00:17:32,370
This feels just like Leon coming back to Raccoon City.

157
00:17:33,100 --> 00:17:35,300
I didn't even know this room existed.

158
00:17:35,700 --> 00:17:38,200
Not that knowing would do a guy like you any good.

159
00:17:38,530 --> 00:17:42,600
So how about you help me tidy up.

160
00:17:42,600 --> 00:17:46,330
Clean fast, then off to class. Busted on day one.

161
00:17:46,900 --> 00:17:48,930
All because of you, jock.

162
00:17:48,930 --> 00:17:52,270
Yes, dear friend Physics. The second it's manual labor,

163
00:17:52,270 --> 00:17:53,370
it's always me, huh.

164
00:17:53,370 --> 00:17:55,230
Why not make Fuen do it?

165
00:17:56,430 --> 00:17:58,370
Nah, he doesn't have to.

166
00:18:01,930 --> 00:18:02,970
Put that down.

167
00:18:04,870 --> 00:18:08,600
Just wipe the dust off these books, that's all.

168
00:18:09,470 --> 00:18:11,770
Then I'll go fill the bucket with water.

169
00:18:16,230 --> 00:18:19,500
With love and respect, from your friend Physics.

170
00:18:19,900 --> 00:18:21,200
Do the honors, friend Aof.

171
00:18:22,100 --> 00:18:23,200
Of course, dearest friend.

172
00:18:24,400 --> 00:18:26,870
What kind of friendship standard is this?

173
00:18:26,870 --> 00:18:28,900
So damn unequal, seriously.

174
00:18:29,330 --> 00:18:30,600
I'm getting goosebumps, man.

175
00:18:30,600 --> 00:18:32,270
Whatever, whatever.

176
00:18:32,270 --> 00:18:33,930
Just do your job.

177
00:18:35,000 --> 00:18:36,500
Ugh, the dust.

178
00:18:44,930 --> 00:18:48,600
Fuen, I think luck's on your side today.

179
00:18:48,600 --> 00:18:49,930
Come here a sec.

180
00:18:50,330 --> 00:18:51,330
Yeah, coming.

181
00:18:51,330 --> 00:18:52,270
What is it?

182
00:18:55,670 --> 00:18:58,870
Star. M.5. The pride of Class King.

183
00:18:59,870 --> 00:19:02,030
Yeah, I know.

184
00:19:03,530 --> 00:19:07,570
♪ Could I be into you? It's you, only you ♪

185
00:19:07,570 --> 00:19:11,300
♪ Like you've put me under a spell ♪

186
00:19:12,000 --> 00:19:19,130
♪ One look at you and I'm gone, my whole heart, out of control ♪

187
00:19:20,800 --> 00:19:21,600
Whoa.

188
00:19:22,330 --> 00:19:24,170
So freaking cute.

189
00:19:25,900 --> 00:19:28,270
How is someone this cute?

190
00:19:29,100 --> 00:19:31,930
A second ago this room was pitch dark.

191
00:19:31,930 --> 00:19:33,900
Now it's blindingly bright.

192
00:19:35,470 --> 00:19:37,200
So fucking dramatic.

193
00:19:38,300 --> 00:19:40,870
There, I turned on the lights. Bright enough?

194
00:19:40,870 --> 00:19:43,030
I didn't mean the lights in the room.

195
00:19:43,030 --> 00:19:44,730
I meant the light in my heart.

196
00:19:45,330 --> 00:19:47,930
How can you not see how cute he is?

197
00:19:49,400 --> 00:19:50,600
This cute.

198
00:19:51,500 --> 00:19:52,700
This into him.

199
00:19:53,700 --> 00:19:55,630
Then go for it, why don't you.

200
00:20:00,600 --> 00:20:03,170
Physics, you're my only hope.

201
00:20:03,170 --> 00:20:04,130
You're my God.

202
00:20:04,130 --> 00:20:05,570
You're my father.

203
00:20:07,030 --> 00:20:08,330
Oh, my bro.

204
00:20:09,270 --> 00:20:11,330
Please, help me.

205
00:20:14,130 --> 00:20:17,070
But right now, I think you've lost it.

206
00:20:17,270 --> 00:20:17,970
Whoa—

207
00:20:18,230 --> 00:20:21,530
Physics, don't be so cruel to your friend.

208
00:20:23,200 --> 00:20:25,600
Fuen, you know what?

209
00:20:26,300 --> 00:20:29,300
Physics is a damn smooth flirt.

210
00:20:30,500 --> 00:20:34,670
When he's after someone, the target never even notices.

211
00:20:35,630 --> 00:20:39,570
Even right now, the guy he's after has no clue.

212
00:20:41,500 --> 00:20:42,970
But if you don't believe me,

213
00:20:43,930 --> 00:20:45,600
get Physics...

214
00:20:46,800 --> 00:20:48,470
to help you win Star over.

215
00:20:48,670 --> 00:20:49,700
You asshole, Aof.

216
00:20:50,170 --> 00:20:53,700
Whoa, you're really that good?

217
00:20:53,700 --> 00:20:55,830
How did I never know this?

218
00:20:56,700 --> 00:21:01,230
Ugh, Physics, help me win him over, please.

219
00:21:05,270 --> 00:21:07,870
Hmm...

220
00:21:07,870 --> 00:21:08,900
No.

221
00:21:09,630 --> 00:21:13,470
I barely even asked. Why're you saying no already?

222
00:21:14,130 --> 00:21:16,630
You're hoarding your secrets. Selfish.

223
00:21:17,270 --> 00:21:19,130
I'm not hoarding anything.

224
00:21:19,130 --> 00:21:20,800
I just don't want to help you flirt.

225
00:21:23,100 --> 00:21:24,530
Dear Mr. Physics, sir.

226
00:21:25,070 --> 00:21:27,300
Mr. Physics, hear me out.

227
00:21:28,670 --> 00:21:32,600
This is our final year, man! / Mm-hmm.

228
00:21:32,600 --> 00:21:36,000
We graduate soon. If Mr. Physics won't help Mr. Fuen

229
00:21:36,000 --> 00:21:40,130
win Star over now, then when will he ever, right?

230
00:21:40,130 --> 00:21:43,530
So, Mr. Physics—

231
00:21:44,330 --> 00:21:47,500
help Mr. Fuen win Star over, please.

232
00:21:48,100 --> 00:21:50,500
Don't be so heartless to your friend.

233
00:21:51,300 --> 00:21:52,600
Dearest friend.

234
00:21:54,830 --> 00:21:57,400
Come on... Physics.

235
00:21:58,430 --> 00:22:01,900
If you help me and it doesn't work out,

236
00:22:01,900 --> 00:22:04,300
I won't say a single word against you.

237
00:22:04,300 --> 00:22:07,430
I just want to try once. Please, man.

238
00:22:15,670 --> 00:22:18,330
After listening to Aof—

239
00:22:18,930 --> 00:22:23,000
he said this is our final year, right?

240
00:22:23,870 --> 00:22:28,070
Say you actually win Star over. That'd be bad.

241
00:22:28,070 --> 00:22:29,600
Because then you might not get to see Star.

242
00:22:29,600 --> 00:22:31,300
I think that'd be really sad.

243
00:22:32,230 --> 00:22:34,570
You just told me to go for him a second ago.

244
00:22:35,900 --> 00:22:36,730
I was being sarcastic.

245
00:22:36,730 --> 00:22:39,730
Wait, sarcastic for what?

246
00:22:39,730 --> 00:22:42,000
Come on, help me win him over.

247
00:22:42,430 --> 00:22:43,670
Please.

248
00:22:44,000 --> 00:22:45,600
I'm begging you, Physics.

249
00:22:48,530 --> 00:22:49,730
Alright, alright.

250
00:22:51,200 --> 00:22:52,300
Dear friend Fuen.

251
00:22:52,730 --> 00:22:56,670
There's one thing I want to tell you.

252
00:22:58,130 --> 00:22:59,000
I'm not helping.

253
00:22:59,500 --> 00:23:03,230
Hey, wait—Physics, Physics!

254
00:23:03,430 --> 00:23:05,970
Physics, please help me.

255
00:23:07,000 --> 00:23:09,070
Physics! Physics!

256
00:23:10,400 --> 00:23:12,570
Aof—Aof, help me out!

257
00:23:12,700 --> 00:23:13,530
I'm busy.

258
00:23:13,530 --> 00:23:15,130
Physics, I'm begging you.

259
00:23:15,530 --> 00:23:17,930
I'll do your cleaning duty for you.

260
00:23:17,930 --> 00:23:20,370
This room's a damn mess. / Physics!

261
00:23:25,130 --> 00:23:29,070
That concludes my presentation. Thank you.

262
00:23:34,630 --> 00:23:37,470
Tinnaphat, that was a great presentation.

263
00:23:37,470 --> 00:23:39,270
Oh, it wasn't just me, sir.

264
00:23:39,600 --> 00:23:42,870
I have to thank my group mates too.

265
00:23:42,870 --> 00:23:45,030
On my own, I'd never have made it.

266
00:23:45,500 --> 00:23:46,430
Sir,

267
00:23:46,430 --> 00:23:48,070
may I say something to my friends?

268
00:23:58,870 --> 00:24:06,030
Guys, this is the last year we'll all be together.

269
00:24:07,670 --> 00:24:09,770
We've been together so long.

270
00:24:12,900 --> 00:24:15,200
I want us to make good memories.

271
00:24:16,630 --> 00:24:19,230
And help each other out.

272
00:24:20,200 --> 00:24:21,730
And finally—

273
00:24:23,000 --> 00:24:24,930
anyone who won't help me,

274
00:24:25,500 --> 00:24:26,900
I'll consider not so lovable.

275
00:24:31,930 --> 00:24:33,530
Go take your seat.

276
00:24:33,530 --> 00:24:34,570
Thank you, sir.

277
00:24:50,470 --> 00:24:51,700
This is your doing, isn't it.

278
00:24:52,200 --> 00:24:53,900
I only meant well.

279
00:24:53,900 --> 00:24:54,970
Don't believe me? Ask Fuen.

280
00:24:54,970 --> 00:24:55,600
Yeah.

281
00:24:56,100 --> 00:24:59,430
Physics, help me win him over. I really like him.

282
00:24:59,430 --> 00:25:00,230
Please.

283
00:25:05,000 --> 00:25:08,300
Tang, look, he won't even pay attention to me.

284
00:25:08,530 --> 00:25:10,030
Help me talk to him, would you?

285
00:25:10,030 --> 00:25:12,730
Ugh, if he doesn't want to, don't force him.

286
00:25:12,730 --> 00:25:14,870
And don't listen to Aof so much.

287
00:25:15,230 --> 00:25:17,330
He can't even handle his own love life.

288
00:25:17,770 --> 00:25:19,630
I'm handling it fine. I just haven't started.

289
00:25:21,470 --> 00:25:23,000
You bastard.

290
00:25:26,070 --> 00:25:29,130
Alright, that's it for today. See you next class.

291
00:25:29,470 --> 00:25:31,870
Thank you, sir.

292
00:25:47,230 --> 00:25:51,870
Physics, I really do like Star.

293
00:25:55,100 --> 00:25:57,230
If not you, then who, Physics?

294
00:25:59,100 --> 00:26:03,370
If it's not you, no one else can help me.

295
00:26:03,370 --> 00:26:06,900
You're my closest friend.

296
00:26:07,700 --> 00:26:09,730
If not you, then who?

297
00:26:09,730 --> 00:26:11,600
These two clowns?

298
00:26:11,600 --> 00:26:13,970
No way. It has to be you, man.

299
00:26:15,230 --> 00:26:16,630
Please.

300
00:26:18,430 --> 00:26:21,530
Hey, say something, help me out.

301
00:26:21,530 --> 00:26:24,800
You know best how much I like him. He's so cute.

302
00:26:24,800 --> 00:26:26,300
Friends help each other, come on.

303
00:26:26,370 --> 00:26:27,600
No, friend.

304
00:26:32,670 --> 00:26:33,530
Then—

305
00:26:35,600 --> 00:26:37,170
I'll even get on my knees.

306
00:26:37,170 --> 00:26:38,000
Fuen.

307
00:26:39,870 --> 00:26:41,070
I'm not helping.

308
00:26:41,400 --> 00:26:42,430
Physics!

309
00:26:43,000 --> 00:26:45,200
Dear friend, where are you going?

310
00:26:50,800 --> 00:26:52,000
What the fuck!

311
00:26:53,600 --> 00:26:54,800
This is all your fault.

312
00:26:55,700 --> 00:26:57,130
Let's just go eat.

313
00:26:58,030 --> 00:26:59,170
Physics!

314
00:27:00,030 --> 00:27:00,730
Physics!

315
00:27:01,300 --> 00:27:02,630
Physics, wait up!

316
00:27:05,270 --> 00:27:07,330
Hey, just help me out.

317
00:27:08,930 --> 00:27:10,530
I'm exhausted here.

318
00:27:43,500 --> 00:27:45,400
If I help you, what do I get?

319
00:27:45,800 --> 00:27:47,200
Anything you want.

320
00:27:47,700 --> 00:27:50,300
Whatever you want, it's yours.

321
00:27:54,270 --> 00:27:56,070
You sure you'll give me anything?

322
00:27:56,070 --> 00:27:56,970
Mm-hmm.

323
00:27:58,270 --> 00:27:59,870
So what do you want?

324
00:28:14,470 --> 00:28:17,930
Alright, class, today we'll continue with the exercises.

325
00:28:17,930 --> 00:28:22,500
Turn to page 51, line 7, paragraph 3.

326
00:28:22,500 --> 00:28:24,530
Today we'll pick up with...

327
00:28:27,700 --> 00:28:30,230
Physics, do this right.

328
00:28:30,230 --> 00:28:33,600
Won't he think we're creepy stalkers?

329
00:28:33,600 --> 00:28:37,070
Hey! I'm not telling you to just stare, okay?

330
00:28:37,070 --> 00:28:40,230
Before you go after someone, you've got to know them first.

331
00:28:40,230 --> 00:28:44,330
Honestly, did you ever know what Star does at school all day?

332
00:28:44,330 --> 00:28:45,230
Huh?

333
00:28:45,230 --> 00:28:47,000
During class, though?

334
00:28:47,470 --> 00:28:49,000
That's straight-up creepy.

335
00:28:49,930 --> 00:28:52,070
Then quit questioning it.

336
00:28:52,070 --> 00:28:54,270
Just do as I say.

337
00:28:55,730 --> 00:28:57,500
So what do I do next?

338
00:28:57,500 --> 00:29:00,570
Keep spying until I know everything about him?

339
00:29:00,800 --> 00:29:01,600
Look.

340
00:29:01,600 --> 00:29:04,000
That's the coward's way.

341
00:29:04,000 --> 00:29:05,300
But first—

342
00:29:07,130 --> 00:29:09,800
quit being so nervous and act normal.

343
00:29:09,800 --> 00:29:10,330
Okay.

344
00:29:11,700 --> 00:29:17,500
First, we check how he sees you.

345
00:29:18,030 --> 00:29:19,730
How? I'm getting nervous again.

346
00:29:19,730 --> 00:29:20,330
Hey.

347
00:29:20,730 --> 00:29:22,300
I said don't be nervous.

348
00:29:22,930 --> 00:29:24,730
Alright, here's what you'll do.

349
00:29:24,730 --> 00:29:26,300
Try walking past his classroom.

350
00:29:26,530 --> 00:29:29,130
If you're really on his radar,

351
00:29:30,300 --> 00:29:32,300
he'll look at you no matter what.

352
00:29:33,230 --> 00:29:33,730
Got it.

353
00:29:36,300 --> 00:29:37,800
Don't be stiff.

354
00:29:37,800 --> 00:29:39,130
Don't come off as a bore.

355
00:29:39,130 --> 00:29:42,300
This isn't just a casual stroll.

356
00:29:42,300 --> 00:29:46,570
You're walking to catch his attention.

357
00:29:47,330 --> 00:29:51,170
Basically, you're making yourself known to him.

358
00:29:52,000 --> 00:29:53,600
And the moment he looks at you,

359
00:29:54,330 --> 00:29:55,770
that's when you slay.

360
00:29:55,770 --> 00:29:57,230
Slay.

361
00:29:58,500 --> 00:30:00,000
You can count on this.

362
00:30:00,770 --> 00:30:02,230
I'm confident. I can totally do this.

363
00:30:41,530 --> 00:30:42,930
What do you want me to look at?

364
00:30:48,530 --> 00:30:49,800
Where're you going?

365
00:31:07,630 --> 00:31:08,530
Hnngh.

366
00:31:13,700 --> 00:31:20,000
"You're so cute. I wanna talk to you."

367
00:31:26,670 --> 00:31:27,930
Fuen, what are you doing here?

368
00:31:27,930 --> 00:31:30,130
"You're so cute. I wanna talk to you."

369
00:31:30,130 --> 00:31:32,030
"You're so cute. I wanna talk to you."

370
00:31:32,030 --> 00:31:32,800
Who's that?

371
00:31:33,330 --> 00:31:34,070
Who is that?

372
00:31:35,670 --> 00:31:36,300
Who's there?

373
00:31:36,400 --> 00:31:38,300
"You're so cute. I wanna talk to you."

374
00:31:38,800 --> 00:31:40,300
Who was that just now?

375
00:31:40,900 --> 00:31:41,970
Who was it? Satayu?

376
00:31:41,970 --> 00:31:43,930
I don't know either, teacher.

377
00:31:44,230 --> 00:31:46,130
Don't let the teacher catch on, Satayu.

378
00:31:46,130 --> 00:31:47,330
Yeah, yeah.

379
00:32:19,130 --> 00:32:20,730
How's he ever gonna look at me now?

380
00:32:20,730 --> 00:32:25,270
Probably fine—just maybe a little unexpected.

381
00:32:26,030 --> 00:32:27,770
Are you actually comforting me?

382
00:32:28,670 --> 00:32:30,170
So insincere.

383
00:32:30,170 --> 00:32:31,670
I can see you laughing at me.

384
00:32:33,900 --> 00:32:35,400
See, you're still laughing.

385
00:32:35,400 --> 00:32:37,100
Fine, I'm out of here.

386
00:32:38,800 --> 00:32:42,400
Hey, hey, calm down.

387
00:32:43,330 --> 00:32:46,070
I only laugh because you're too adorable.

388
00:32:55,330 --> 00:32:57,130
So? Giving up yet?

389
00:32:59,270 --> 00:33:02,630
Trust me, this just isn't your thing.

390
00:33:03,970 --> 00:33:07,730
No! You promised you'd help me.

391
00:33:08,000 --> 00:33:09,800
If this method doesn't work,

392
00:33:10,700 --> 00:33:12,600
then find me a new one.

393
00:33:15,870 --> 00:33:17,530
You—Tinnaphat.

394
00:33:17,530 --> 00:33:19,230
Physics.

395
00:33:19,230 --> 00:33:20,700
Follow me right now.

396
00:33:21,030 --> 00:33:21,900
Come with me.

397
00:33:22,500 --> 00:33:23,800
Come on, over here.

398
00:33:31,770 --> 00:33:33,430
Arms out.

399
00:33:34,330 --> 00:33:34,830
Hurry up.

400
00:33:35,200 --> 00:33:37,930
Arms out, one leg up.

401
00:33:38,700 --> 00:33:39,530
Good.

402
00:33:40,100 --> 00:33:42,000
And both of you, bite down on this ruler.

403
00:33:42,000 --> 00:33:44,100
So you don't go causing trouble for others.

404
00:33:44,100 --> 00:33:45,500
Understood?

405
00:33:59,000 --> 00:34:00,000
Is this really right?

406
00:34:00,600 --> 00:34:02,400
The teacher said to bite the ruler.

407
00:34:03,030 --> 00:34:04,430
Like this?

408
00:34:04,970 --> 00:34:05,830
Mm-hmm.

409
00:34:05,830 --> 00:34:07,070
You sure?

410
00:34:07,070 --> 00:34:08,330
Sure.

411
00:34:08,330 --> 00:34:09,330
Okay.

412
00:34:20,800 --> 00:34:21,670
Ow!

413
00:34:22,600 --> 00:34:24,469
When you play innocent, you really commit, Physics.

414
00:34:24,469 --> 00:34:25,270
Huh—

415
00:34:25,270 --> 00:34:27,130
Who bites down on the same ruler?

416
00:34:27,130 --> 00:34:27,870
I knew it.

417
00:34:27,870 --> 00:34:30,570
Stop it, quit playing it cool. On your feet.

418
00:34:31,330 --> 00:34:32,530
Bite down.

419
00:34:34,830 --> 00:34:37,230
And hold that until the period's over.

420
00:34:37,230 --> 00:34:38,330
Yes, ma'am.

421
00:34:38,330 --> 00:34:41,100
You just love causing trouble, don't you.

422
00:34:47,300 --> 00:34:49,199
Wanna just ditch?

423
00:34:49,199 --> 00:34:50,830
I'm too lazy to keep standing.

424
00:34:52,100 --> 00:34:53,730
Sure, why not.

425
00:34:55,500 --> 00:34:56,900
Let's bail.

426
00:35:07,370 --> 00:35:08,970
Chemi.

427
00:35:09,270 --> 00:35:10,930
Which club are you joining?

428
00:35:11,930 --> 00:35:13,530
I still can't decide.

429
00:35:13,530 --> 00:35:18,170
But one thing's for sure—no sports.

430
00:35:18,830 --> 00:35:21,370
Hey, but you've gotta stick with me.

431
00:35:21,800 --> 00:35:23,300
Don't ditch me.

432
00:35:23,300 --> 00:35:24,800
Hey, no way.

433
00:35:24,800 --> 00:35:28,400
We've gotta stay together. We can't split up.

434
00:35:29,100 --> 00:35:31,230
What would we even do in a soccer club?

435
00:35:31,230 --> 00:35:33,730
Chemi's gasping for air just from running.

436
00:35:37,400 --> 00:35:41,570
I want to stay with you guys, but I can't play soccer.

437
00:35:41,570 --> 00:35:45,000
Does your club have anything besides soccer?

438
00:35:49,130 --> 00:35:50,570
Ow, Tang, that hurt.

439
00:35:56,100 --> 00:35:57,370
Oh, hey, Jay.

440
00:35:57,700 --> 00:35:58,470
Hi there!

441
00:35:58,470 --> 00:36:00,330
See you at the club today. Don't be late.

442
00:36:01,200 --> 00:36:02,470
Got it!

443
00:36:16,330 --> 00:36:18,700
My club's all athletes right now.

444
00:36:18,700 --> 00:36:20,930
Barely any staff. We're super short-handed.

445
00:36:20,930 --> 00:36:23,570
And second term there's the traditional football match.

446
00:36:23,570 --> 00:36:27,100
And Aof's probably playing his final year—the M.6 seniors.

447
00:37:09,300 --> 00:37:11,000
Thank you for looking out for me.

448
00:37:23,000 --> 00:37:24,230
535.

449
00:37:27,600 --> 00:37:28,830
536.

450
00:37:34,600 --> 00:37:35,830
540.

451
00:37:41,330 --> 00:37:42,930
Am I strong?

452
00:37:59,100 --> 00:37:59,900
Chemi!

453
00:38:03,130 --> 00:38:04,330
Watch out!

454
00:38:07,600 --> 00:38:10,200
I told you, didn't I? Football's dangerous.

455
00:38:23,870 --> 00:38:25,930
♪ No matter how the story goes ♪

456
00:38:25,930 --> 00:38:29,330
♪ In the end, my answer is you ♪

457
00:38:34,430 --> 00:38:37,330
I told you—I'll protect you, Chemi.

458
00:38:39,430 --> 00:38:40,700
Thank you.

459
00:38:42,200 --> 00:38:44,270
♪ No matter how the story goes ♪

460
00:38:44,270 --> 00:38:47,670
♪ In the end, my answer is you ♪

461
00:38:55,900 --> 00:38:57,500
You're sure about this?

462
00:38:59,770 --> 00:39:02,430
You guys know how much I love football.

463
00:39:02,430 --> 00:39:03,870
Which team do you support?

464
00:39:03,870 --> 00:39:05,230
Who's your favorite player?

465
00:39:05,230 --> 00:39:07,770
Where's the next World Cup?

466
00:39:08,670 --> 00:39:10,770
I don't know.

467
00:39:12,600 --> 00:39:14,130
But what I do know for sure

468
00:39:14,130 --> 00:39:16,100
is I'm joining this club.

469
00:39:16,100 --> 00:39:17,330
Easy there.

470
00:39:17,330 --> 00:39:18,830
Hold on a sec.

471
00:39:19,470 --> 00:39:21,300
So does your club have anything else to do?

472
00:39:21,300 --> 00:39:22,900
I'm sure they'll find you something.

473
00:39:25,900 --> 00:39:26,830
Then—

474
00:39:28,230 --> 00:39:29,730
I'm in this club.

475
00:39:30,500 --> 00:39:34,130
"Chemi"

476
00:39:50,230 --> 00:39:51,570
Tuck in your shirt, please.

477
00:40:16,470 --> 00:40:17,500
Hey.

478
00:40:17,500 --> 00:40:19,500
Cleaning up the basketballs after you two is exhausting.

479
00:40:19,800 --> 00:40:20,930
Of course it is.

480
00:40:20,930 --> 00:40:22,530
You just gamed all break, never went anywhere.

481
00:40:22,530 --> 00:40:24,130
I even asked you to Siam and you couldn't be bothered.

482
00:40:24,130 --> 00:40:25,100
Run it off, man.

483
00:40:25,100 --> 00:40:28,430
Wow, who's as eager to leave the house as you?

484
00:40:28,430 --> 00:40:30,500
Seven days a week, you're out six.

485
00:40:30,500 --> 00:40:33,130
Can't help it. There's nothing to do at home.

486
00:40:33,130 --> 00:40:36,700
When I go to Physics, he won't let me over—he's glued to Fuen, dammit.

487
00:40:36,700 --> 00:40:38,930
When I come to you, you won't come out.

488
00:40:39,230 --> 00:40:40,330
And you—

489
00:40:40,830 --> 00:40:42,230
when you're not tutoring, you're studying.

490
00:40:42,230 --> 00:40:45,430
Not everyone's got an athlete's quota like you.

491
00:40:45,430 --> 00:40:47,300
Just cruising through every day.

492
00:40:48,730 --> 00:40:51,930
Plus my mom wants me at the same university she went to.

493
00:40:59,700 --> 00:41:00,430
Look at you.

494
00:41:01,200 --> 00:41:03,770
Just thinking about those university scores gives me goosebumps.

495
00:41:06,400 --> 00:41:08,330
But I'm rooting for you, man.

496
00:41:08,330 --> 00:41:11,300
Even if I don't really get why your mom's so serious

497
00:41:11,300 --> 00:41:13,570
about the university over the major you actually want.

498
00:41:16,770 --> 00:41:19,970
Oh, and... Fuen and Physics didn't come play?

499
00:41:24,000 --> 00:41:25,000
It's Physics—

500
00:41:25,000 --> 00:41:26,670
he's helping Fuen chase the pride of Class King.

501
00:41:29,900 --> 00:41:30,900
You mean Star?

502
00:41:33,500 --> 00:41:35,230
Star's the pride of Class King.

503
00:41:35,230 --> 00:41:37,100
And you're the monkey of my class.

504
00:41:37,100 --> 00:41:38,330
Go collect the balls.

505
00:41:38,700 --> 00:41:40,630
Me again? I'm an athlete, you know.

506
00:41:42,000 --> 00:41:43,730
Oh, the star athlete.

507
00:42:05,430 --> 00:42:08,730
Man... I don't think I'm ready to see him.

508
00:42:08,730 --> 00:42:10,670
If you're not ready, let's just go back.

509
00:42:11,330 --> 00:42:13,570
If trying to win someone over

510
00:42:13,570 --> 00:42:15,670
stresses you out this much, I say drop it.

511
00:42:16,670 --> 00:42:19,100
When you were chasing that person, weren't you stressed?

512
00:42:20,330 --> 00:42:22,670
Nah. They were adorably clueless.

513
00:42:23,400 --> 00:42:24,970
The person I'm after, I mean.

514
00:42:24,970 --> 00:42:30,130
Ugh, you won't even introduce me, but you'll still brag.

515
00:42:38,500 --> 00:42:41,530
You say I brag—when did I ever brag?

516
00:42:41,530 --> 00:42:45,070
It was just Aof and his big mouth.

517
00:42:45,070 --> 00:42:48,270
If I win him over, I'll brag to you every single day.

518
00:42:48,270 --> 00:42:49,870
Pfft. Someone like you?

519
00:42:49,870 --> 00:42:52,430
Without my help, you'd never pull it off.

520
00:42:52,430 --> 00:42:54,330
Is that a challenge?

521
00:43:16,430 --> 00:43:19,300
Man, this means I got rejected, right?

522
00:43:21,500 --> 00:43:23,700
If we're being realistic—

523
00:43:24,630 --> 00:43:25,400
yeah, buddy.

524
00:43:25,400 --> 00:43:26,300
But it's okay.

525
00:43:26,300 --> 00:43:29,470
Because in the end, you've got a friend like me. Come on, let's go home.

526
00:43:29,900 --> 00:43:32,300
Then I'll treat you to dinner to cheer you up.

527
00:43:32,300 --> 00:43:33,670
Fuen...

528
00:43:44,930 --> 00:43:48,800
When you came by my classroom, did you need something?

529
00:43:50,170 --> 00:43:52,830
I, uh... help me out here.

530
00:43:55,900 --> 00:44:01,330
Oh, Fuen here wants your contact, Star.

531
00:44:02,330 --> 00:44:05,200
But you already have my Instagram.

532
00:44:05,730 --> 00:44:08,170
And we're following each other, right?

533
00:44:08,430 --> 00:44:11,030
Right... we're following?

534
00:44:15,270 --> 00:44:19,370
It's more that he wants your Line, Star.

535
00:44:19,370 --> 00:44:21,130
But that's probably a no, right?

536
00:44:21,130 --> 00:44:27,630
Since you've got that whole rule about giving out your Line.

537
00:44:29,430 --> 00:44:33,230
Oh, right! The pride-of-Class-King thing?

538
00:44:36,300 --> 00:44:37,730
Oh, that rule?

539
00:44:39,570 --> 00:44:45,370
But for you, Fuen, of course I can.

540
00:44:46,000 --> 00:44:46,800
Huh?!

541
00:44:47,030 --> 00:44:48,500
You'd really give it to me, Star?

542
00:44:48,500 --> 00:44:49,530
Of course.

543
00:45:03,530 --> 00:45:05,800
Here you go. / Thank you so much.

544
00:45:07,170 --> 00:45:09,530
I should get going now.

545
00:45:09,530 --> 00:45:11,430
I've got tutoring to rush to.

546
00:45:11,430 --> 00:45:12,670
Okay.

547
00:45:13,900 --> 00:45:15,100
See you.

548
00:45:15,470 --> 00:45:17,030
Travel safe.

549
00:45:19,030 --> 00:45:20,030
Bye.

550
00:45:34,670 --> 00:45:36,100
You gonna keep waving forever?

551
00:45:37,330 --> 00:45:40,430
If you were a beauty queen, you'd score a perfect ten right now.

552
00:45:41,330 --> 00:45:42,630
I'm just happy, okay?

553
00:45:43,570 --> 00:45:46,870
Who knew your plan would work this well?

554
00:45:47,000 --> 00:45:48,270
Hey!

555
00:45:50,000 --> 00:45:52,470
Come on, what do you wanna eat? My treat.

556
00:45:54,900 --> 00:45:57,500
Hmm... I wanna watch a movie.

557
00:45:57,500 --> 00:45:59,530
Sure, Siam?

558
00:46:01,130 --> 00:46:01,830
My place.

559
00:46:01,830 --> 00:46:03,670
Alright! Let's do it, buddy.

560
00:46:14,500 --> 00:46:15,670
Hmm.

561
00:46:15,670 --> 00:46:18,100
Was it really that big a deal?

562
00:46:21,930 --> 00:46:24,570
I've just never been that close to him before.

563
00:46:25,870 --> 00:46:27,970
And especially when our eyes met—

564
00:46:28,930 --> 00:46:31,400
I was so nervous he'd notice how flustered I was.

565
00:46:34,300 --> 00:46:39,030
Time, do you think I should message him first?

566
00:46:42,400 --> 00:46:45,500
Up to you. Do you want to?

567
00:46:48,900 --> 00:46:51,900
It's his final year, after all.

568
00:46:51,900 --> 00:46:54,130
I don't want to waste any time.

569
00:46:55,930 --> 00:46:59,470
Then message him after tutoring, I'd say...

570
00:46:59,470 --> 00:47:03,730
Something this important is better said face to face.

571
00:47:17,000 --> 00:47:19,130
Hey... what are you filming?

572
00:47:19,670 --> 00:47:22,730
Come on, Star blushing is a rare sight—gotta get it on camera.

573
00:47:22,730 --> 00:47:25,830
Samai, let's head out.

574
00:47:57,630 --> 00:47:59,570
So do you actually want to watch this movie?

575
00:48:00,700 --> 00:48:04,830
You keep staring at me instead. How can you even follow it?

576
00:48:09,300 --> 00:48:10,630
Because of you, that's why.

577
00:48:11,370 --> 00:48:12,230
Huh?

578
00:48:13,930 --> 00:48:15,930
I'm just sitting here watching.

579
00:48:19,400 --> 00:48:24,830
Or are you upset that I'm chasing Star?

580
00:48:32,570 --> 00:48:34,470
Holy shit...

581
00:48:40,300 --> 00:48:42,300
You like Star too, don't you?

582
00:48:45,870 --> 00:48:50,400
Fuen, I know you're dumb,

583
00:48:51,070 --> 00:48:54,870
but this time it's a bit too much.

584
00:48:54,870 --> 00:48:58,770
Well... if that's not it—

585
00:49:01,070 --> 00:49:06,200
Oh... or are you being possessive of me?

586
00:49:07,570 --> 00:49:12,870
You're scared that if I get a boyfriend, I won't be around you.

587
00:49:12,870 --> 00:49:14,970
Whoa... afraid of being lonely, huh.

588
00:49:16,930 --> 00:49:18,170
Just leave me alone.

589
00:49:27,400 --> 00:49:32,070
Suit yourself. But don't come saying I don't care about you.

590
00:49:32,070 --> 00:49:35,200
I care about you like crazy.

591
00:49:44,200 --> 00:49:48,330
Even if I get a boyfriend, you've got that person of yours.

592
00:49:49,830 --> 00:49:53,530
So even without me, you won't be lonely.

593
00:49:55,030 --> 00:49:56,000
Win-win, right?

594
00:50:00,530 --> 00:50:04,400
So who is this person? Can you tell me?

595
00:50:08,270 --> 00:50:11,800
Well... it's been several years now.

596
00:50:13,300 --> 00:50:18,630
Cute, but a bit of a space case.

597
00:50:18,900 --> 00:50:23,500
Huh, so why aren't you two together yet?

598
00:50:29,530 --> 00:50:33,970
Or are you afraid I'd get lonely?

599
00:50:47,830 --> 00:50:50,570
Do you have a photo of them? Let me see.

600
00:50:51,030 --> 00:50:52,130
Hey, Fuen!

601
00:50:52,830 --> 00:50:55,370
Let me see, just one photo, that's all.

602
00:50:55,370 --> 00:50:56,070
Hey!

603
00:50:56,070 --> 00:50:57,630
Do I know them? Let me see.

604
00:50:57,630 --> 00:50:58,370
Hey!

605
00:51:02,530 --> 00:51:03,500
Come here.

606
00:51:07,000 --> 00:51:08,270
Get up, come here.

607
00:51:12,230 --> 00:51:13,770
Take a photo with me first.

608
00:51:13,770 --> 00:51:14,600
No way.

609
00:51:14,600 --> 00:51:17,070
And why are you so protective of it anyway?

610
00:51:17,070 --> 00:51:19,630
Aof knows, even Tang knows, right?

611
00:51:19,630 --> 00:51:22,130
Come here. / Why am I the only one who doesn't?

612
00:51:22,930 --> 00:51:25,270
Would you quit asking so much.

613
00:51:26,270 --> 00:51:31,130
Fine—sit still, take a photo with me, and I'll tell you.

614
00:51:32,230 --> 00:51:33,500
Okay.

615
00:51:37,670 --> 00:51:40,900
One, two—oops!

616
00:51:44,100 --> 00:51:45,370
What was that?

617
00:51:46,100 --> 00:51:49,530
Ugh, that photo's gonna come out ridiculous.

618
00:51:51,070 --> 00:51:52,030
Let me see it.

619
00:51:52,030 --> 00:51:52,770
What?

620
00:51:53,800 --> 00:51:57,330
Physics, hand it over, let me see.

621
00:52:01,170 --> 00:52:02,130
No, no.

622
00:52:02,530 --> 00:52:03,800
No, no.

623
00:52:06,930 --> 00:52:08,970
Then reach for it. Can you reach?

624
00:52:08,970 --> 00:52:10,470
Can you reach it? Can you?

625
00:52:12,500 --> 00:52:13,730
Hey, wait, wait.

626
00:52:15,900 --> 00:52:19,230
The stuff I taught you—what did you take away?

627
00:52:20,730 --> 00:52:23,500
The flirting lesson? Of course I got it.

628
00:52:25,600 --> 00:52:26,830
Which is?

629
00:52:28,600 --> 00:52:36,400
That if you like someone, you try to get yourself close to them.

630
00:52:37,830 --> 00:52:43,270
Act natural, don't stress, and don't be stiff.

631
00:52:44,400 --> 00:52:48,670
Mm-hmm. What else did you get?

632
00:52:50,670 --> 00:52:51,730
I got...

633
00:52:53,470 --> 00:52:54,800
Star's Line.

634
00:52:57,600 --> 00:52:58,670
Fuen!

635
00:52:59,070 --> 00:53:01,100
Okay, kidding.

636
00:53:02,900 --> 00:53:03,830
I got...

637
00:53:04,400 --> 00:53:05,370
you got...

638
00:53:05,930 --> 00:53:07,170
I don't know.

639
00:53:12,630 --> 00:53:13,870
Here.

640
00:53:15,670 --> 00:53:17,100
Give me your hand.

641
00:53:26,470 --> 00:53:28,630
When you like someone,

642
00:53:30,330 --> 00:53:34,400
you just put yourself close to them.

643
00:53:35,830 --> 00:53:41,330
By any means—as long as they don't feel uncomfortable.

644
00:53:53,730 --> 00:53:54,870
Get it?

645
00:53:59,470 --> 00:54:00,600
Oh...

646
00:54:02,330 --> 00:54:05,600
So if I want to get closer to Star, then...

647
00:54:09,530 --> 00:54:10,670
Close.

648
00:54:13,600 --> 00:54:14,470
Oh!

649
00:54:15,730 --> 00:54:18,200
Dude! Star's calling!

650
00:54:18,770 --> 00:54:19,630
Oh, and...

651
00:54:20,070 --> 00:54:21,800
Today's definitely my day.

652
00:54:22,170 --> 00:54:23,730
Hello, Star.

653
00:54:23,730 --> 00:54:24,970
Huh, and what about me?

654
00:54:26,570 --> 00:54:27,830
Hello, Fuen.

655
00:54:27,830 --> 00:54:29,470
What's up?

656
00:54:29,470 --> 00:54:31,130
Where are you right now, Fuen?

657
00:54:31,130 --> 00:54:34,700
I'm at a friend's place. What's up, Star? Something wrong?

658
00:54:34,700 --> 00:54:36,530
I just really want to see you.

659
00:54:40,270 --> 00:54:42,170
But if you're busy, then...

660
00:54:42,170 --> 00:54:44,770
No, no, I'm free! Where are you?

661
00:54:44,770 --> 00:54:46,570
Where are you right now? I'll come to you.

662
00:54:46,570 --> 00:54:48,430
I'm at Siam.

663
00:54:48,430 --> 00:54:52,700
Okay, I'll head over. That's it for now, I'm on my way. Bye.

664
00:54:55,300 --> 00:54:57,730
Wait, you're going to see Star right now?

665
00:54:58,830 --> 00:55:01,270
You're the one who told me. Closer.

666
00:55:01,570 --> 00:55:06,570
If you like someone, you put yourself close to them.

667
00:55:06,930 --> 00:55:09,070
But wait... you're not done talking with me.

668
00:55:10,730 --> 00:55:13,770
We'll... talk tomorrow, okay? See ya!

669
00:55:14,070 --> 00:55:17,230
Wait—your bike?

670
00:55:17,970 --> 00:55:19,330
It's with me.

671
00:55:19,530 --> 00:55:20,530
I'll take the BTS.

672
00:55:21,030 --> 00:55:22,400
The motorbike's not cool.

673
00:55:22,830 --> 00:55:25,470
Once the helmet's off, my hair looks like a baby goat.

674
00:55:25,970 --> 00:55:28,300
Then I'll come too. / See you tomorrow, tomorrow!

675
00:55:36,700 --> 00:55:39,030
He ditched me and the bike.

676
00:55:46,800 --> 00:55:51,470
♪ When you turn to me, I can't hold your gaze for long ♪

677
00:55:51,470 --> 00:55:57,530
♪ I dream of it every night, but I can't do a thing ♪

678
00:55:57,530 --> 00:56:02,930
♪ The look in your eyes leaves my heart trembling ♪

679
00:56:02,930 --> 00:56:07,270
♪ One slip and my mind wanders off ♪

680
00:56:08,100 --> 00:56:18,100
♪ I've handed you my heart, I steal a glance every day, I can't take it ♪

681
00:56:18,770 --> 00:56:24,100
♪ By your side every day, yet I must act indifferent ♪

682
00:56:24,100 --> 00:56:29,630
♪ We stay just friends, so I keep it locked inside ♪

683
00:56:29,630 --> 00:56:35,170
♪ I want you to know, but I can't cross that line ♪

684
00:56:35,170 --> 00:56:40,700
♪ I know what's between us should stay hidden ♪

685
00:56:52,100 --> 00:56:57,400
♪ Afraid that if I speak, you'll never look at me the same ♪

686
00:56:57,400 --> 00:57:02,900
♪ Afraid that one day, the bond between us will break ♪

687
00:57:02,900 --> 00:57:08,400
♪ Should I say it out loud, or let it stay a dream? ♪

688
00:57:08,400 --> 00:57:12,630
♪ One slip and my mind wanders off ♪

689
00:57:15,230 --> 00:57:16,330
Oh, Fuen.

690
00:57:17,530 --> 00:57:21,200
I'm sorry for asking to meet so suddenly.

691
00:57:22,630 --> 00:57:25,370
It's totally fine. No problem at all.

692
00:57:27,830 --> 00:57:34,600
So... I have something important to tell you. It means a lot to me.

693
00:57:34,870 --> 00:57:37,870
One sec, Star. Let me brace myself for a moment.

694
00:57:43,200 --> 00:57:45,330
Okay, I'm ready.

695
00:57:45,730 --> 00:57:50,570
I've thought it through—I have to tell you this to your face.

696
00:57:51,630 --> 00:57:54,530
But this won't put you in a tough spot, will it?

697
00:57:55,030 --> 00:57:57,970
Not at all. You can tell me anything, Star.

698
00:57:58,600 --> 00:58:00,300
So...

699
00:58:02,770 --> 00:58:05,130
I like Physics.

700
00:58:07,530 --> 00:58:09,970
Fuen, could you help me win Physics over?

701
00:58:15,170 --> 00:58:17,600
It's totally fine. No problem at all...

702
00:58:26,700 --> 00:58:28,530
Here it comes.

703
00:58:30,530 --> 00:58:32,670
Mmm... smells amazing, Mom.

704
00:58:32,670 --> 00:58:34,200
Eat it all up.

705
00:58:37,170 --> 00:58:38,030
Mom.

706
00:58:38,730 --> 00:58:39,600
Yes, dear?

707
00:58:44,930 --> 00:58:46,870
I want to sleep over at Fuen's.

708
00:58:48,070 --> 00:58:50,000
Still haven't won Fuen over, honey?

709
00:59:01,930 --> 00:59:07,770
Soon we graduate and go our separate ways. Gonna let that time go to waste?

710
00:59:07,770 --> 00:59:13,000
Only the smooth ones rule the world.

711
00:59:13,500 --> 00:59:17,630
I like Physics. Can you help me with this? Please.

712
00:59:18,200 --> 00:59:19,900
Where'd you leave your soul?

713
00:59:23,930 --> 00:59:26,830
You three again? Get ready for detention.

714
00:59:26,830 --> 00:59:29,300
If I've liked you for a long time and I want to court you—

715
00:59:29,300 --> 00:59:32,070
I want you to notice me. What would make you most comfortable?

716
00:59:32,070 --> 00:59:34,830
Just bring yourself close to me, that's enough.

717
00:59:35,170 --> 00:59:37,830
But if it's not Star, it really can't be anyone else.

718
00:59:37,830 --> 00:59:39,970
Going to Din—someone that disciplined—

719
00:59:39,970 --> 00:59:42,130
it has to be Star. It can't be anyone else.

720
00:59:42,130 --> 00:59:46,400
My friends are all in this club. Off on my own, I'd be so lonely.

721
00:59:46,400 --> 00:59:49,100
But I had a lot of fun today.

722
00:59:49,600 --> 00:59:52,730
Chemi, after practice today—don't rush off, okay?

723
00:59:57,500 --> 00:59:58,500
Hey! Fuen!
